# Plan-execute auto-continue

When working this repo's Cursor plan (`.cursor/plans/*.plan.md`) or when the user says `plan-execute`:

## End of every agent turn (mandatory)

1. Run:
   ```bash
   node scripts/plan-execute-handoff.mjs --write-next
   ```
2. If you discovered missing plan work, write `.cursor/plan-execute.gaps.json` then:
   ```bash
   node scripts/plan-execute-handoff.mjs --scan-gaps --apply-gaps
   node scripts/plan-execute-handoff.mjs --write-next
   ```
3. Read `.cursor/plan-execute.next.json` — its `agentInstructions` and `nextSteps` are the SSOT for what comes next.

## Auto-continue

- Enable with `bash scripts/plan-execute-enable.sh` (creates `.cursor/plan-execute.active`).
- Post-MVP: `bash scripts/plan-execute-enable.sh --through-all` (also creates `.cursor/plan-execute.through-all`) so stop-hook continues after MVP until `all-complete`.
- On each agent **stop**, the stop hook: validates prior (`pnpm test` + `--check`) → applies gaps → writes `next.json` → emits `followup_message`.
- If prior validation **fails**, the follow-up is **fix prior** (do not advance packages).
- Disable with `bash scripts/plan-execute-disable.sh`.

## Skills

Follow `.cursor/skills/plan-execute/SKILL.md` for REQ→AC→TEST→EDGE ticks. Do not invent packages; use `--check` / HOW TO when format breaks.

## Fail closed

No silent skips. Failed tests → do not mark plan todos completed. Corrupt gaps file → fix or delete; do not invent todos without `[NN/M][KIND]` tags.
